From 9651a8729df84059b4fe0f476932155f6483501b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 19:18:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/15] [B70][XPU][MoE] W4A8 grouped GEMM: int8 per-token
 activations x int4 g128 experts, s8 x s4 DPAS

cutlass_grouped_gemm_w4a8 (Xe2): the routed-expert grouped GEMM of
cutlass_grouped_gemm_xe2 with the mixed-precision DPAS atom
XE_DPAS_TT<8, int32_t, int8_t, int4_t> (dpas.s4.s8). The int4 weights are
the bytes XpuFusedMoe holds after implement_zp ([E, N, K/2], bf16 scales
[E, N, K/128]) and feed the systolic array as nibbles: no unpack, no repack.
A is int8 [M, K] with one fp32 scale per row. Each 128-wide K group
accumulates in int32; at the group end the partial is converted and scaled
by w_scale[n, g] into an fp32 accumulator (a twin bf16 TiledMMA supplies
the identical f32 C layout and the D store); the row scale and optional
bias are applied once before the bf16 store.

- csrc/xpu/grouped_gemm/xe_2_w4a8: mainloop + persistent grouped launcher,
  policies 128x256 / 32x64 / 16x64 / 8x64 by average rows per expert (as
  W4A16), tile K 64 (B70_W4A8_TILE_K=32 for one atom), g128, bf16 out.
- _xpu_C.cutlass_grouped_gemm_w4a8 (linked library grouped_gemm_w4a8_xe_2)
  and an opt-in standalone module _b70_w4a8_C (-DB70_W4A8_STANDALONE=ON /
  env B70_W4A8_STANDALONE=1) loadable next to an installed wheel.
- vllm_xpu_kernels/b70_moe_w4a8.py: quantize token rows once, route int8
  bytes + scales through the stock remap, gemm1, SiLU, per-row quant,
  gemm2, stock moe_gather. XpuFusedMoe.apply(..., w4a8=True) uses it.
- tests/b70/t_w4a8_cutlass.py: GPU exactness vs float64, MoE vs fp32 and
  stock W4A16, microbench at per-rank shapes of a 512-expert MoE.

